URBIX Community Code of Conduct

Our Commitment

URBIX is an international project built around transparency, collaboration, innovation, and respect.

We are committed to creating a welcoming environment for everyone, regardless of experience, nationality, background, or technical ability.

Expected Behavior

All community members are expected to:

- Treat everyone with respect and professionalism.
- Communicate honestly and constructively.
- Welcome different opinions and technical discussions.
- Give credit to other contributors.
- Avoid harassment, discrimination, threats, and personal attacks.
- Respect the project's security and privacy guidelines.

Unacceptable Behavior

The following behavior is not acceptable:

- Harassment, intimidation, or discrimination.
- Publishing private information without permission.
- Fraud, impersonation, or deliberate misinformation.
- Malicious code or attempts to compromise accounts and systems.
- Manipulating project discussions or misrepresenting project progress.

Reporting Problems

Report conduct violations privately to the project maintainers through an appropriate private communication channel.

Do not publish passwords, private keys, seed phrases, or sensitive personal information.

Enforcement

Project maintainers may review reports and take proportionate action, including warnings, removal of inappropriate content, or restriction of participation.

Scope

This Code of Conduct applies to URBIX project spaces, repositories, discussions, and official community channels.

Project Status

URBIX is an evolving project. Community governance and enforcement procedures may be refined as the project grows.
